    "title": "Risk Factors for Hyperglycemia with DTG",
    "message": "Guidelines recommend screening for hyperglycemia risk factors before initiating or transitioning to DTG. Risk factors include age ≥30 years, family history of DM, hypertension, or BMI ≥25 Kg/m². The patient is 38 years old (≥30). Her BMI is not calculated but her weight is stable at 64kg; height is not provided to assess BMI. The urinalysis shows 'glucose trace', which is a potential sign of hyperglycemia. The clinician's plan is blank, so screening and management are not addressed.",
